# Diagrams

A fence that opens `d2#show` or `mermaid#show` is a **diagram cell**. The
preview draws it, and keeps its source one click away behind **Code**. Edit a
cell and the drawing follows as you type.

Each drawing has three small buttons at its top right edge: smaller, the
current size, and larger. The middle one puts the drawing back at its own
size.

More diagram types are on [[mermaid-gallery]], and the states a cell can be in
are on [[states]].

## The same picture in both languages

In Mermaid:

```mermaid#show
flowchart LR
  client -->|credentials| edge
  edge -->|verify| auth
  auth -->|token| edge
  edge -->|token + rotation window| client
```

In D2:

```d2#show
direction: right

client -> edge: credentials
edge -> auth: verify
auth -> edge: token
edge -> client: token + rotation window
```

## A listing is not drawn

A plain `mermaid` fence shows Mermaid source as text. It is how a card
explains the notation without turning the example into a picture.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  shown --> as-code
```

## A plain `d2` fence still draws

It has no cell layout, only the drawing and its zoom buttons.

```d2
before -> cells
```

